ac3forge provides CMake targets via find_package(ac3forge):

    find_package(ac3forge CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE ac3::forge)

Every other library is a separate, opt-in feature - none installed by default, since each adds its
own public API, CMake targets and binaries. When present, their own targets are also available:

    matroska  ->  matroska::matroska  (Matroska/.mkv)
    mp4       ->  mp4::mp4            (MP4/ISOBMFF, plus fMP4/CMAF + HLS/DASH)
    mpegts    ->  mpegts::mpegts      (MPEG-2 Transport Stream)
    capi      ->  ac3::forge_c        (C11 API over the codec)
    ac4       ->  ac4::decoder, ac4::encoder, ac4::ac4  (AC-4 decoding, encoding and reading)
    iab       ->  ac3iab::ac3iab      (SMPTE ST 2098-2 Immersive Audio Bitstream reading)
    iamf      ->  iamf::iamf          (IAMF writing)

    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE matroska::matroska mp4::mp4 mpegts::mpegts)

To install the three container writers alongside the codec:

    vcpkg install ac3forge[matroska,mp4,mpegts]

Or pick any subset, e.g. AC-4 only:

    vcpkg install ac3forge[ac4]
